---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
import ReaderDiscovery from '../components/ReaderDiscovery.astro';
import '../styles/story-home-feature.css';
---
<Site title="Yorùbá Stories & Living Memories" active="Overview">
  <section class="hero wrap">
    <div>
      <p class="kicker">OUR STORIES · OUR BELIEFS · OUR VOICES</p>
      <h1>Every town has a tale.<br/><em>What did yours tell you?</em></h1>
      <p class="lead">An evening story you never forgot. A name your grandmother explained. A mystery the whole town remembers differently. Come and hear Yorùbá voices, then discover another telling.</p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="button" href="/tales/">Enter the stories <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        <a class="button secondary" href="/figures/">Explore beliefs &amp; figures</a>
      </div>
      <p class="fine">Original stories are clearly labelled; living community contributions will appear with the teller’s permission.</p>
    </div>
    <figure class="home-editorial-cover home-story-feature">
      <div class="story-fire-scene" role="img" aria-label="Decorative imagined evening storytelling scene: warm lantern light beneath a large tree, with the silhouettes of a storyteller and listeners.">
        <span class="story-fire-moon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span class="story-fire-tree" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span class="story-fire-horizon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span class="story-fire-people" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>
        <span class="story-fire-glow" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span class="story-fire-words" lang="yo" aria-hidden="true">Àlọ́ o!</span>
      </div>
      <figcaption>
        <p class="kicker">TONIGHT'S STORY · MỌ́REMÍ ÀJÀṢORÒ</p>
        <h2><a href="/tales/moremi-fire-in-the-reeds/">The night the forest<br/><em>kept a secret.</em></a></h2>
        <p>A city is afraid. A woman follows the danger into the reeds—and discovers that courage may ask for more than anyone can give.</p>
        <p><a class="home-feature-link" href="/tales/moremi-fire-in-the-reeds/">Enter Mọ́remí's story <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></p>
        <p class="fine">An original dramatic retelling, not a recorded elder's testimony. Accounts of Mọ́remí differ by teller and community.</p>
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <ReaderDiscovery/>
  <section class="wrap section" aria-labelledby="home-tales">
    <div class="section-title">
      <div><p class="kicker">START WITH A STORY</p><h2 id="home-tales">What happens next?</h2></div>
      <p class="muted">A rumour, a mysterious traveller and a question about a name. Three complete stories to get the conversation started.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="collection-grid">
      <a class="collection" href="/tales/laughing-mask/">
        <span class="kicker">ORIGINAL FICTION · GẸ̀LẸ̀DẸ́-INSPIRED</span>
        <h3>Who Was the Laughing Mask Talking About?</h3>
        <p>A twelve-second video turns a town upside down. Was the rumour ever the real story?</p>
        <span class="text-link">Read the tale ↗</span>
      </a>
      <a class="collection" href="/tales/esu-hat-two-views/">
        <span class="kicker">IMAGINATIVE RETELLING · ÈṢÙ</span>
        <h3>The Hat That Divided the Road</h3>
        <p>Two friends witness the same traveller. How can both be so certain—and so angry?</p>
        <span class="text-link">Read the tale ↗</span>
      </a>
      <a class="collection" href="/tales/olodumare-many-meanings/">
        <span class="kicker">ORIGINAL FICTION · OLÓDÙMARÈ</span>
        <h3>The Name That Would Not Fit Into One Answer</h3>
        <p>One name, several meanings, and the explanations children carry home from different people.</p>
        <span class="text-link">Read the tale ↗</span>
      </a>
    </div>
    <p class="home-story-link"><a class="text-link" href="/tales/">Explore Stories &amp; Living Memories →</a></p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap notice" aria-labelledby="home-beliefs">
    <p class="kicker">THE NAMES PEOPLE GROW UP HEARING</p>
    <h2 id="home-beliefs">Who is Èṣù? Who is Ọ̀ṣun?</h2>
    <p>Discover the roles, names, beliefs and sacred stories people share about Èṣù, Olódùmarè, Ọ̀ṣun, Ògún, Ṣàngó and other figures. Hear what different families and communities understand without requiring every telling to end in the same conclusion.</p>
    <a href="/figures/">Meet the òrìṣà and remembered figures →</a>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap section" aria-labelledby="home-places">
    <div class="section-title">
      <div><p class="kicker">WHERE THE STORIES LIVE</p><h2 id="home-places">Every place remembers.</h2></div>
      <p class="muted">Towns, rivers, markets and neighbourhoods carry names, legends and memories that deserve to be told by the people who know them.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="collection-grid">
      <a class="collection" href="/places/"><span class="kicker">PLACES &amp; THEIR VOICES</span><h3>Follow a town’s story</h3><p>Start with a place. What did families say about its beginnings? Which telling travelled further?</p><span class="text-link">Explore places ↗</span></a>
      <a class="collection" href="/community/"><span class="kicker">YOUR VERSION MATTERS</span><h3>What did you hear growing up?</h3><p>Maybe an elder told you another version. Maybe you witnessed something worth remembering. Every voice can add a chapter.</p><span class="text-link">Visit Community Voices ↗</span></a>
      <a class="collection" href="/learning/"><span class="kicker">READ, TALK, LEARN</span><h3>Keep the conversation going</h3><p>Explore Yorùbá words, language and questions to discuss with family, friends and other curious readers.</p><span class="text-link">Explore learning ↗</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Site>